</subsection>
<subsection xml:id="subsec-exploratory-visualizations">
<title>Exploratory Data Analysis: "Plots First"</title>
<p> Before computing p-values or fitting regression coefficients, a data-first approach demands visual inspection of empirical distributions, group contrasts, and bi-variate relationships. We present three critical diagnostic views of the flamingo data. </p>
<p>
<m>\textbf{1. Between-Habitat Variation (The Distributional View)}</m>
: When examining
<m>\texttt{plumage\_index}</m>
across the three lakes, we observe a dramatic rightward shift in distributions from Nakuru to Bogoria to Natron.
</p>
<table xml:id="table-summary-stats">
<title>Summary Statistics of Carotenoid Plumage Index and Spirulina Density by Lake Habitat</title>
